{
 "duration": 78.289,
 "phrases": [
  {
   "text": "This is a Roman warship... and a city wall is picking it up.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 5.386
  },
  {
   "text": "Rewind.",
   "start": 5.813,
   "end": 6.599
  },
  {
   "text": "Syracuse, 213 BC. Before dawn, Rome's fleet creeps toward the city walls.",
   "start": 6.947,
   "end": 13.619
  },
  {
   "text": "The plan: get so close that the city's catapults... shoot right over their heads. And it works.",
   "start": 14.101,
   "end": 20.808
  },
  {
   "text": "Then, above them... something creaks.",
   "start": 21.061,
   "end": 23.598
  },
  {
   "text": "A huge beam swings out over the wall... and lowers an iron hand on a chain.",
   "start": 23.867,
   "end": 30.153
  },
  {
   "text": "It grabs the ship by the nose.",
   "start": 30.471,
   "end": 32.533
  },
  {
   "text": "Behind the wall, the far end of the beam is pushed down, like a seesaw... and the front of the ship rises.",
   "start": 32.853,
   "end": 40.673
  },
  {
   "text": "Higher... until it's standing on its stern.",
   "start": 41.089,
   "end": 43.957
  },
  {
   "text": "Then... they let go.",
   "start": 44.222,
   "end": 44.984
  },
  {
   "text": "Some ships capsized. Most just filled with water.",
   "start": 45.409,
   "end": 49.245
  },
  {
   "text": "The genius behind it wasn't a general. He was a mathematician in his seventies: Archimedes.",
   "start": 49.544,
   "end": 55.983
  },
  {
   "text": "The Roman commander joked that Archimedes was using his ships to scoop up seawater... His men didn't laugh.",
   "start": 56.308,
   "end": 63.272
  },
  {
   "text": "One ancient writer says that whenever a rope or a stick poked over the wall, they screamed...",
   "start": 63.512,
   "end": 69.69
  },
  {
   "text": "THERE IT IS!",
   "start": 69.932,
   "end": 70.777
  },
  {
   "text": "...and fled.",
   "start": 71.081,
   "end": 71.897
  },
  {
   "text": "Rome stopped attacking the walls. It just waited... because of one old man.",
   "start": 72.326,
   "end": 78.087
  }
 ],
